  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Architectural/Structural Design A.S. Degree - Local GE' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published September 17, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7616/PublishedPdf). GE Pattern: SCC Local AA/AS. Official Total Units: 60-63; this seed models the first-listed/recommended path = 13 + 16 + 15 + 16 = 60 units (ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page; Major Electives at 3 units each). Semester sums verified against the map's 13-14 / 16 / 15 / 16-18 headers. Choice slots: (1) ENGL C1000 / ENGL H+ 488 / ESLW 340, Local Area L1A — ENGL C1000 selected; (2) INDIS 313 / HCD 310, Local Area L7B Life Development Skills — INDIS 313 selected; (3) Math: 'Choose one of the recommended courses under your STEM placements' (check eServices; meet with a counselor) — modeled as 'Any Local Area L2 course'; (4) Major Elective — a minimum of 6 units, choose 2 courses: EDT 332, EDT 336, EDT 340, EDT 342, EDT 352, EDT 356, MATH 373, SURVY 300, SURVY 310 — EDT 332 and EDT 336 selected (first-listed options, no unmet prereqs: EDT 332 requires EDT 310 or concurrent enrollment). In-plan prereqs: EDT 312 requires EDT 310 (taken 1st 8 weeks, then EDT 312 2nd 8 weeks); EDT 316 requires EDT 310; EDT 320 requires EDT 310 or equivalent (may be taken concurrently); EDT 317 requires EDT 310 — all with grades of 'C' or better. Documented prereqs for options not selected: EDT 352 requires EDT 310 or concurrent enrollment; MATH 373 requires Intermediate Algebra or equivalent (Integrated Math 3) with 'C-' or better or placement (STEM 3/5 placement levels not eligible); SURVY 310 requires EDT 310. Placement prereqs (documented): students not placing directly in ENGL C1000 take the ENGL 80/ENGL C1000 combo; ENGL 488 requires ESL 325 with a 'C' or better; ESLW 340 requires ESL 325 or Los Rios assessment placement. AA requirements: 60 degree-applicable units with 2.0 GPA, 12 units within Los Rios, each required course 'C' or better, SCC local GE Areas L1A, L1B, L2, L3, L4, L5, L6, L7A, L7B. Electives: any courses numbered 100-499. Engineering Design Technology — Science, Math, & Engineering Meta Majors. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
